          "body": "## Problem\n`Taskfile.yml`'s `auto:`/`arm:`/`agent:` blocks set `env: AGENT_CMD: '{{.AGENT_CMD | default \"\"}}'`. A shell-exported `AGENT_CMD` is shadowed, the run completes on the default driver, and `write-handoff.mjs` banks a record attributed to whatever driver actually ran. Nothing tells the operator. Hub note: `agent-cmd-is-a-taskfile-var-not-an-env-var`. Same shape for `SCENARIO_ID` (three threading paths, inconsistent defaults on standalone `quiesce`) and `PROVIDER` (Taskfile default `\"\"`, `agent-agy.sh` default `antigravity`).\n\nUnder ADR-0029 an unlabelled or mislabelled run is not evidence, so this is a measurement bug, not a DX nit.\n\n## Change\n1. Taskfile `env:` blocks fall back to the process env when no Taskfile var is passed (`{{.AGENT_CMD | default (env \"AGENT_CMD\")}}` or equivalent), for `AGENT_CMD`, `RUNNER`/`AGENT_MODE`, `SCENARIO_ID`, `PROVIDER`, `AGY_MODEL`.\n2. `scripts/auto-incident.mjs` prints one resolved-config banner before arming: `AGENT_CMD RUNNER SCENARIO_ID PROVIDER MODEL CONFINEMENT`, and refuses to arm when `AGENT_CMD` is empty and `RUNNER=external`.\n3. Same banner content is what `write-handoff.mjs` stamps, so the banner and the record cannot disagree.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `AGENT_CMD=bash scripts/agent-agy.sh pnpm forge auto booklogr` (shell export, no Taskfile arg) runs the agy driver and the banked record says `harness: agy`.\n- A test in `tools/transcript/test/` or the Taskfile smoke that fails when the banner's driver and the record's `harness` differ.\n\nFiles: `use-cases/booklogr/stacks/flask-compose/Taskfile.yml`, `scripts/auto-incident.mjs`, `tools/transcript/write-handoff.mjs`.",
