          "url": "https://github.com/prismalens/sreforge/issues/172",
          "truncated": false
        },
        {
          "number": 173,
          "title": "P0.2 ops: agy driver preflight \u2014 fail in seconds on missing srt, unauthenticated agy, or WSL mirrored networking",
          "body": "## Problem\n`scripts/agent-agy.sh` starts a run capped at `--print-timeout 45m0s`. Three known preconditions fail silently and only surface as empty stdout at the end: `srt` not on PATH, `agy` weekly quota or auth gone, WSL mirrored networking blackholing srt egress (the script's own header comment). Hub notes: `agy-gemini-quota-cycles`, `sandbox-runtime-tanstack-evaluation`, `agent-driver-tiers`.\n\n## Change\nA preflight block at the top of `agent-agy.sh` (or a shared `scripts/preflight-agy.sh` called from `doctor.mjs` too) that checks, in order, and exits non-zero with a one-line reason:\n- `srt` resolvable and runnable\n- `agy` authenticated (cheapest call that proves it, and distinguishes quota-exhausted from unauthenticated)\n- WSL networking mode is NAT (read `/etc/wsl.conf` or `wslinfo --networking-mode`)\n- `PROVIDER` non-empty and present in `infra/agent-sandbox/providers.json`\n\nWrite the preflight result into the handoff so a record can never come from a run whose preflight was skipped.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Unset PATH entry for srt \u2192 exit within 5 s, message names srt.\n- `pnpm forge doctor` runs the same checks and reports them.",
          "labels": [
